[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Mechanical derivation
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every non-comment line of the entire C library (`c_src/src/driver.c`, after
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m resolving digraphs `%:`→`#`, `<%`→`{`, `%>`→`}`):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m #include "driver.h"
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m #include <stdio.h>
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m #include <iso646.h>
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m void driver(int x, int y) {
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     int result = x | ~y;   /* x bitor compl y */
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     printf("%d", result);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     puts("");
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m }
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Greps run over `c_src/` for every rejection mechanism:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | searched for | matches in C source |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|---|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `return` (any) | 0 |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `return -1` / `return NULL` / `RETURN_ERROR` / error macros | 0 |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `assert` | 0 |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `errno` | 0 |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `exit(` / `abort` | 0 |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `if` / `switch` / `goto` / loops | 0 |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | relational / range checks (`<`, `>`, `<=`, `>=`) | 0 |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | null-pointer checks | 0 (the API takes no pointers) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | min/max constants (`INT_MAX`, `LIMIT`, `MAX_`, `MIN_`) | 0 |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | error enums / status types | 0 (`driver` returns `void`) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Result: the C library has an EMPTY intrinsic error surface.** `driver` is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `void`, takes two by-value `int`s, performs a total (never-trapping) bitwise
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m expression, and unconditionally prints. There is no input it rejects and no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m channel (return value, out-param, errno, enum) through which it could report
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m one. Consequently the rows below are the *generic FFI boundaries every C API
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m has*, as required by Phase C: extremes, one-step-past-range values, degenerate
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m values, and out-of-range "enum-like" integers. For each, the correct C
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m behaviour is **no rejection** — and the differential test asserts that the Rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m also does not reject, i.e. both print the identical bytes and both return
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m normally (no panic, no abort, no trap).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 1 | `driver` | `x = 0, y = 0` — degenerate all-zero input | no error; `~0 = -1`, `0 \| -1 = -1`; prints `-1\n`; returns void |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 2 | `driver` | `x = 0, y = -1` — the only pair whose result is `0` (falsy/sentinel-looking value) | no error; prints `0\n` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 3 | `driver` | `x = INT_MIN (-2147483648)`, `y = 0` — extreme low `x`, sign bit set | no error; prints `-1\n` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 4 | `driver` | `x = INT_MAX (2147483647)`, `y = 0` — extreme high `x` | no error; prints `-1\n` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 5 | `driver` | `y = INT_MIN` — `~INT_MIN = INT_MAX`, complement of the extreme low value | no error; prints `x \| 0x7FFFFFFF` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 6 | `driver` | `y = INT_MAX` — `~INT_MAX = INT_MIN`, complement produces the sign bit | no error; prints `x \| INT_MIN` (always negative) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 7 | `driver` | `x = 0, y = INT_MAX` — result is exactly `INT_MIN`, a magnitude with no positive `int` counterpart (the classic negation-overflow trap for `%d` formatting) | no error; prints `-2147483648\n` (11 bytes + newline) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 8 | `driver` | `x = INT_MIN, y = INT_MIN` — both operands extreme low | no error; `INT_MIN \| INT_MAX = -1`; prints `-1\n` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 9 | `driver` | `x = INT_MAX, y = INT_MAX` — both operands extreme high | no error; `INT_MAX \| INT_MIN = -1`; prints `-1\n` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 10 | `driver` | one step past the top of the signed range: caller passes `0x80000000` as an unsigned 32-bit bit pattern (wraps to `INT_MIN` across the FFI boundary) | no error; identical to row 3's `x`; prints per `x \| ~y` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 11 | `driver` | one step past the bottom: caller passes `0x7FFFFFFF + 1` computed by wrapping arithmetic | no error; same as row 10 |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 12 | `driver` | out-of-range "enum-like" integers: values that would have no valid variant if the parameters were enums — `x`/`y` ∈ {`-2147483648`, `-1000000`, `-2`, `3`, `42`, `255`, `256`, `65536`, `2147483647`} in all 81 combinations. C enums accept any `int`, so these are real inputs. | no error for any combination; each prints `x \| ~y` then newline |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 13 | `driver` | sign-bit-only operands: `x = 0x80000000`, `y = 0x80000000` (single high bit) | no error; prints `-1\n` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 14 | `driver` | single-bit sweep: `x = 1<<i`, `y = 1<<j` for all `i, j` in `0..32` (includes `1<<31` = `INT_MIN`) — 1024 combinations, every bit position including the sign bit | no error for any pair; prints `x \| ~y` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 15 | `driver` | repeated invocation without intervening flush (state/buffer reuse across many back-to-back calls) | no error; outputs concatenate in call order, one line each |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 16 | `driver` | *no* null-pointer row is possible — `driver` accepts no pointer arguments (verified: 0 `*` parameters in `driver.h`); the nearest analogue is passing the null bit pattern `0` for both scalars, i.e. row 1 | n/a |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 17 | `driver` | *no* length/size row is possible — `driver` accepts no buffer or length argument, so "zero length" and "oversized length" are inexpressible; the nearest analogues are rows 1–2 (zero) and rows 3–4 (extreme magnitude) | n/a |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rows 16 and 17 are recorded explicitly so the absence of null-pointer and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m length checks is documented as a *derived fact about the C API's signature*,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m not as an untested gap.
