[49m[38;5;10m+     1[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # CONFIGS.md — Phase B configuration-surface table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Mechanical derivation of the axes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Full public API (`c_src/include/driver.h`, digraphs resolved):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m #ifndef DRIVER_H_
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m #define DRIVER_H_
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m void driver(int x, int y);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m #endif
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Public entry points:** exactly one — `driver`. It is simultaneously the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   lowest-level and the highest-level entry point; there is no convenience
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   wrapper and no lower layer to reach past. `nm -D` confirms `driver` is the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   only exported symbol (see `SYMBOLS.md`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Runtime options / modes / flags:** none. Greps for `if`, `switch`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `#ifdef`, and for any global/static state in `c_src/` return 0 matches; the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   function has no configuration parameters, no setters, and no persistent
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   state.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Compile-time configuration:** none in `CMakeLists.txt` beyond
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `add_library(driver SHARED src/driver.c)`; no `option()`, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `target_compile_definitions`. `translation/Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   section, so the Rust side has one build configuration only.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The remaining axes are therefore the **input data shapes**, which is where all
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m behaviour variation lives. `int result = x | ~y;` then `printf("%d", result)`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m is data-dependent in these ways the code/libc distinguish:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **A. sign of `result`** — controls whether `%d` emits a `-`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **B. decimal width of `result`** — 1..10 digits (11 bytes with the sign),
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   controls the emitted byte count.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **C. sign bit of each operand** (`x` and `y` independently) — `~y` moves the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   sign bit, and `|` with a negative operand forces `result` negative.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **D. extreme values** `INT_MIN` / `INT_MAX` / `0` / `-1` — `-1` is the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   all-ones identity for `|`, `0` is the identity, `INT_MIN` is the only
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   magnitude with no positive `int` counterpart.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **E. algebraic relationships between the operands** — `y == x` (forces
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `result == -1`), `y == ~x` (forces `result == x`), `y == -1` (forces
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `result == x`), `x == 0` (forces `result == ~y`), disjoint vs overlapping
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   bit sets.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **F. bit position** — single-bit operands across all 32 positions, incl. the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   sign bit.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **G. call multiplicity** — one call vs many back-to-back calls in one
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   process, since output goes through the shared `stdout` `FILE` buffer and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `printf`/`puts` are split across two calls (a per-call comparison would miss
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   a wrong flush or a swapped ordering of the number and the newline).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every row below is a combination of these axes that the C treats differently
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (cross-product pruned to distinguishable cases). Rows marked *(random)* are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m property-style: many randomized inputs per row from a fixed-seed xorshift PRNG,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m implemented in `tests/differential.rs`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 1 | `driver` | `x = 0, y = 0` — both identities, result `-1` (all ones, negative, 2 bytes) | [x] |
